From d0568889615949ab49fd3d13ee69620aae42199b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: giteaguy <73799093+irnutsmurt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:31:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] cellPhotoImport: the photo picker -- the player picks a
 picture or backs out

dotheroes beta.6, Cubic.Heroes issue #10. The console's photo import is a system screen over the title: the player
picks a picture from the XMB's photo column, or backs out (RET_CANCEL). The stand-in answered every call with the
newest picture; 3D Dot Game Heroes' ALBUM calls the import again as soon as the player leaves a picture and ends
only on RET_CANCEL, so it showed the same picture again for good (the fade to black, then the snapshot back).

Now the call opens a picker on the save-data screen's picture (ps3emu/osd.h, libs/video/osd_saves.c), as the save
list does: the photo column's pictures newest first, each row a thumbnail (a PNG made once in
<PS3_HDD1_ROOT>/photo_thumbnails, the screen reading PNG only), "Snapshot N", the date, the size and the
dimensions; heading "Album", prompts "View" and "Back" in the player's prompt style. Up/Down choose (held: repeat),
Cross/Start (Enter, Z) picks, Circle (Esc, Backspace, X) backs out; the picker comes back to the picture picked
last. It blocks the calling thread like the save list, reads the pad itself (the title may not poll meanwhile),
intercepts the title's input while open and presents its own picture when the title presents nothing. Nothing to
pick: RET_CANCEL at once, as before. No window (a headless run): RET_CANCEL after 4 s of real time -- 30 s
while a test drives the input (PAD_FILE) -- never a loop.
PS3_PHOTO_IMPORT=<file> still picks that file without the screen. More than 64 pictures: the screen shows a window
of 64 rows around the selection.
