 /*
  * ps3recomp - cellPhotoImport HLE (cellPhotoImportUtil)
  *
- * There is no XMB to pick from, so the pick is the newest JPEG or PNG in the
- * photo column's folder (<PS3_HDD0_ROOT>/photo, where cellPhotoExport puts a
- * title's snapshots), or PS3_PHOTO_IMPORT=<host file> -- copied into the
- * title's directory as the console would. With nothing to pick the answer is
- * RET_CANCEL, the player backing out of the picker. Either way the title's
- * finish callback is queued: 3D Dot Game Heroes' ALBUM waits on it, and with
- * the import unregistered it waited on a black screen for good.
+ * The console's photo import is a system screen over the title: the player
+ * picks a picture from the XMB's photo column, or backs out of it, and the
+ * title's finish callback says which (RET_OK with the picture copied into the
+ * title's directory, or RET_CANCEL). Here the photo column is a folder on the
+ * host (<PS3_HDD0_ROOT>/photo, where cellPhotoExport puts a title's
+ * snapshots) and the screen is the save-data screen's picture (ps3emu/osd.h,
+ * libs/video/osd_saves.c): the pictures as rows, newest first, each with a
+ * thumbnail, its date, size and dimensions; Up/Down choose, Cross (Enter, Z)
+ * picks, Circle (Esc, Backspace, X) backs out. The picker returns to the
+ * picture picked last.
+ *
+ * A title may call it again as soon as the player leaves a picture: 3D Dot
+ * Game Heroes' ALBUM does, and leaves only on RET_CANCEL. The earlier stand-in
+ * answered every call with the newest picture, so the album showed that
+ * picture again for good (Cubic.Heroes issue #10).
+ *
+ * With nothing to pick the answer is RET_CANCEL at once. With no window (a
+ * headless run: nothing can draw the screen, no player to pick) it is
+ * RET_CANCEL after 4 s of real time -- 30 s when a test drives the input
+ * (PAD_FILE): the test is the player then, and its steps may take longer. PS3_PHOTO_IMPORT=<host file> (tests) picks that file
+ * without the screen. Either way the title's finish callback is queued: the
+ * title waits on it, and with the import unregistered it waited on a black
+ * screen for good.
  */
 
